WEBVTT


1
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:07.560
Casting on for 2x2 ribbing
following most knitting machine manuals

2
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.200
can be a bit confusing,
even if you're able to translate

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.680
and follow the instructions, remembering
all the steps can be a challenge.

4
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:25.760
Let's walk through the steps for this cast
on and try to understand what's going on.

5
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:31.040
This plus a cheat sheet is
going to go a long way.

6
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.600
Now, 2x2, ribbing is basic,
there are 2 needles on the main bed,

7
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.840
2 needles and the ribber
alternating across the row.

8
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:48.320
Now, for this caston, you need to make
sure that the END needles are on the main bed

9
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:54.800
add a couple of extra needles from your
instructed cast on number if you need to.

10
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.440
Here's the secret. We're going to be using

11
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.360
two different Ribber positions
for this ribber set up.

12
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.840
The first position is
your knitting position.

13
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:13.640
The Ribber set to P full pitch and the
racking handle is set to position 5.

14
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.480
So the needles are directly
across from each other.

15
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.960
Now, this is what your Ribber is going

16
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.120
to look like when you're
doing the actual knitting.

17
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.800
The other position is the caston position.

18
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.480
You'll set your Ribber to H or half

19
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:44.080
pitch temporarily and you'll rack by one
number during the cast on only.

20
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.560
So let's take a look, I've set my machine
to the knitting position. Again,

21
00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.960
the needles are straight
across from each other.

22
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.600
The needles are on the main bed.

23
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.400
I thread up my machine and I knit across.

24
00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.760
There's no way to hang a cast

25
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.680
on comb, I immediately can
tell that I forgot something.

26
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.920
And that is setting the ribber
to the cast on position.

27
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:32.120
When I set the machine to pitch H
and rack from 5 to 4,

28
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.080
then knit cross,

29
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:40.440
you'll see the strands going across
the opening between the beds.

30
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.920
You'll use these strands
to hang your cast on comb.

31
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.760
Now, these strands are going to be

32
00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.840
the very bottom edge of our ribbing,
so they need to be knitted tightly.

33
00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:08.120
Remember, they're going
to be stretched by the comb.

34
00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.760
So if possible, you'll want to knit this

35
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:16.000
zigzag row at tension zero on both beds.
For a heavier yarn

36
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.080
you may not be able to use tension zero,

37
00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:23.080
but knit as tightly as
you can for a nice edge.

38
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.600
On Brother machines,

39
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.080
it's recommended to use the "two for tiny"
setting on the Ribber carriage.

40
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.560
This will tighten the zigzag
row considerably.

41
00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.200
Look closely, here's another uh oh.

42
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.240
Because you shifted the needles
to the right for the cast on,

43
00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.640
you need to pull up one needle
on the ribber just one little needle

44
00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.520
when you knit that zigzag row.

45
00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.880
You'll cast on this extra stitch.

46
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.000
But we're going to take
care of that in a minute.

47
00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.680
OK, to review, you've selected your two

48
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:19.160
by two, needle set up, casting
on the appropriate number of needles.

49
00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:27.120
Now, set the machine to your cast on set
up. Rack from 5 to 4 and swing

50
00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:34.080
the Ribber to pitch H. You're now
set up in the cast on position.

51
00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.480
Pull that one little lonesome needle
into working position,

52
00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.920
thread up your carriage,
set both carriages to knit as tightly as

53
00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:47.800
possible and knit across. And your
bed should look like this.

54
00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.800
Hang your Ribber comb.

55
00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.400
Now for a perfect selvedge,

56
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:15.800
set your machine to knit on the main bed,
only. The ribber needles should not knit.

57
00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:22.760
Knit across.
You'll be going from left to right.

58
00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:35.560
Next, set your machine to knit on the ribber
only and from right to left.

59
00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:41.400
So you have stitches on the main
bed and stitches on the ribber bed.

60
00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:50.360
Now, set your machine to knit only
on the main bed and knit to the right one more

61
00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:54.760
time. Again, only the main
bed needles are going to knit.

62
00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.560
This completes your cast on.

63
00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.120
Now we want to return the ribber

64
00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.520
to the main knitting position or your
knitting position.

65
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:15.160
That means swing the Ribber to P or
full pitch and rack back to 5.

66
00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.360
Now it's time to retire that one little
extra stitch.

67
00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:24.240
you'll transfer it up from the Ribber
to the main bed,

68
00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.680
doubling up the needle on the left,
on the main bed.

69
00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.160
And we're done with a cast
on position of the ribber.

70
00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.480
Your needles are going to be opposite each

71
00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.480
other and you're going
to continue knitting.

72
00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.720
But wait, wait, wait,
don't start knitting yet.

73
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:48.360
Remember we said everything for a really
tight cast on. Loosen up that tension.

74
00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.080
Following your pattern,

75
00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.800
you may knit your ribbing one or two
numbers tighter than your garment,

76
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.840
but you certainly aren't
going to knit it at zero.

77
00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:03.200
There are so many things
to remember with this technique.

78
00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:08.480
Make yourself a cheat sheet,
my ribber manual isn't really clear.

79
00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:11.840
I always seem to forget a step every time

80
00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:17.720
I try to knit 2x2 ribbing
and the checklist really helps.

81
00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.160
And with all that being said,
there really is a better way.

82
00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.600
How would you like a method where there's

83
00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.760
no racking, no swinging,
no muss, no fuss?

84
00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:36.120
Check out the easiest, best Ribber Caston
in the Knit it Now Learning Library.

85
00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.680
Thank you for watching and happy knitting.

